{"ts": 1791259682.4366, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "What an environment is"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 1, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.26381841230950415}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5894138638965114, "motivation": 0.7346898353259872, "reliance": 0.47698162267354394, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
