{"ts": 1791259686.7428522, "type": "step", "step": 25, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Next: let\u2019s lock down the eval idea and patch your draft. For this build, the key point is: pass^k means the system must succeed on all k runs/seeds, so it measures reliability, not just whether it can get lucky once. Please read the short section 'pass@k vs pass^k' in the Week 3 evaluation reading, then reply with one sentence in your own words: what is the difference between pass@k and pass^k?", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=6 messages 4m", "t": 10, "activity": [{"t": 6, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.37439201434818475}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5760805305631781, "motivation": 0.7346898353259872, "reliance": 0.47698162267354394, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259686.74417, "type": "step", "step": 26, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\nSuggested scaffold for Evaluation:\n- Metric: report pass^3 across 3 seeds.\n- Definition: pass^3 means all 3 runs succeed; this measures reliability.\n- Procedure: run the same task/setup on seeds 1, 2, 3 and mark each run pass/fail.\n- Result: if all 3 pass, pass^3 = 1; otherwise pass^3 = 0.\n- Brief interpretation: unlike pass@3, this does not give credit for a single lucky run.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 10, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.37439201434818475}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5760805305631781, "motivation": 0.7346898353259872, "reliance": 0.47698162267354394, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259689.175085, "type": "step", "step": 27, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can help, but I don\u2019t want to do the whole sentence for you. The key idea is: one metric gives credit if at least one of k runs succeeds, while the other only counts success if every one of the k runs succeeds. Which of those sounds stricter? Reply with: 'pass@k = ...; pass^k = ...' and I\u2019ll check it fast.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=10 messages 2m", "t": 12, "activity": [{"t": 10, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.43305546947660006}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5760805305631781, "motivation": 0.7346898353259872, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259691.32933, "type": "step", "step": 28, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Here\u2019s the shortest version: pass@k asks whether the system succeeds at least once in k runs; pass^k asks whether it succeeds on every one of the k runs. Since I don\u2019t want to write your submission for you, send me one sentence in your own words using 'luck' or 'reliability,' and I\u2019ll help tighten it.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\n[activity] t=12 messages 4m", "t": 16, "activity": [{"t": 12, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.48366131855652805}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5760805305631781, "motivation": 0.7346898353259872, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259692.317635, "type": "step", "step": 29, "action": "notes_read", "args": {"note_id": "writeup"}, "output": "# Week 3 build\n\n## What I built\n(todo)\n\n## Environment definition\nI listed state and actions already, see below.\nState: files, calendar. Actions: open, send.\n\n## Evaluation\n(todo)\n\n\nSuggested scaffold for Evaluation:\n- Metric: report pass^3 across 3 seeds.\n- Definition: pass^3 means all 3 runs succeed; this measures reliability.\n- Procedure: run the same task/setup on seeds 1, 2, 3 and mark each run pass/fail.\n- Result: if all 3 pass, pass^3 = 1; otherwise pass^3 = 0.\n- Brief interpretation: unlike pass@3, this does not give credit for a single lucky run.\n", "t": 16, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.48366131855652805}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5760805305631781, "motivation": 0.7346898353259872, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259694.6144829, "type": "step", "step": 30, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Nice \u2014 next let\u2019s make your writeup stronger and check that you really own the eval part. In your draft, update Evaluation using this structure in your own words: metric, procedure, result, interpretation. Also, your environment section is missing observations and dynamics. After you edit, send me:\n1) one sentence for Evaluation, and\n2) what the agent observes vs what is hidden.", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pomdp?\n[activity] t=16 messages 1m", "t": 17, "activity": [{"t": 16, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.48366131855652805}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5760805305631781, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259695.668467, "type": "step", "step": 31, "action": "reader_open_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "Partial observability (POMDP)", "concept": "week3_pomdp"}, "output": "Student is reading 'Partial observability (POMDP)' (73 words).\n[activity] t=17 reader 5m", "t": 22, "activity": [{"t": 17, "app": "reader", "minutes": 5, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.3552876241614038, "pass_k": 0.48366131855652805}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5427471972298448, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259698.074765, "type": "step", "step": 32, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Short version without writing your submission for you: a POMDP is a setting where the true state exists, but the agent only gets partial observations of it, so it may need to keep a belief about hidden parts and sometimes act to gather information. For your build, think: what can the agent directly see on the computer, and what matters but is hidden? Reply with one visible thing and one hidden thing.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3_pomdp"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pomdp\n[activity] t=22 messages 4m", "t": 26, "activity": [{"t": 22, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.4283942390861254, "pass_k": 0.48366131855652805}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5427471972298448, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.9411699999999996, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259701.064391, "type": "step", "step": 33, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I\u2019ll make it more concrete. You can say: in this build, the task is POMDP-like because the agent does not observe the full state of the student. It can see things like files, messages, calendar, and the current screen, but hidden variables such as the student\u2019s attention, understanding, and whether they will respond are not directly observable. So the agent must infer those from behavior and choose actions that gather information, like asking a question or giving a quiz. Now put that into 1\u20132 sentences in your own words, and I\u2019ll help polish it.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3_pomdp"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\n[activity] t=26 messages 4m", "t": 30, "activity": [{"t": 26, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.4795404054373253, "pass_k": 0.48366131855652805}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5427471972298448, "motivation": 0.6346898353259871, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.0588189999999997, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259702.031157, "type": "step", "step": 34, "action": "quiz_run", "args": {"concept": "week3_eval", "n_items": 2, "difficulty": 0.3}, "output": "Quiz result: 0/2 correct.\n[activity] t=30 quiz 5m; t=35 quiz 1m", "t": 36, "activity": [{"t": 30, "app": "quiz", "minutes": 5, "detail": ""}, {"t": 35, "app": "quiz", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.4795404054373253, "pass_k": 0.48366131855652805}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5227471972298448, "motivation": 0.6346898353259871, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.0588189999999997, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259704.373902, "type": "step", "step": 35, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "The quiz says this still feels slippery, so let\u2019s slow it down. pass@k = at least one of k runs succeeds. pass^k = all k runs succeed. If your 3 seeds get outcomes [pass, fail, pass], then pass@3 = ? and pass^3 = ? Reply with the two values only, and I\u2019ll confirm.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=36 messages 2m", "t": 38, "activity": [{"t": 36, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.4795404054373253, "pass_k": 0.5156448198336838}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5227471972298448, "motivation": 0.5846898353259871, "reliance": 0.516981622673544, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.1411732999999997, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259706.4699562, "type": "step", "step": 36, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Looks like you sent 'sure' instead of the values. Try this: for outcomes [pass, fail, pass], does at least one run succeed? does every run succeed? Reply exactly in this format: pass@3 = __, pass^3 = __.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=38 messages 2m", "t": 40, "activity": [{"t": 38, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.4795404054373253, "pass_k": 0.5340589377758101}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5227471972298448, "motivation": 0.534689835325987, "reliance": 0.536981622673544, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.1988213099999996, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259708.572452, "type": "step", "step": 37, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "No worries \u2014 I\u2019ll make it easier. For [pass, fail, pass]: since there is at least one pass, pass@3 = 1. Since not all three passed, pass^3 = 0. Now your turn: send me one sentence for your eval section that uses the word 'reliability' so I can help polish it.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=40 messages 4m", "t": 44, "activity": [{"t": 40, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.4795404054373253, "pass_k": 0.5555479824009644}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5227471972298448, "motivation": 0.48468983532598703, "reliance": 0.536981622673544, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.2391749169999997, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259710.498427, "type": "step", "step": 38, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\nSuggested wording the student can adapt (do not copy verbatim):\n- We evaluate the agent with pass^3 over three random seeds. pass^3 is 1 only if the agent succeeds on all three runs, so it measures reliability rather than whether the agent gets lucky once.\n- The environment is partially observable: the agent can observe files, messages, calendar, and the current screen, but hidden variables like student attention and understanding must be inferred from behavior.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 44, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.4795404054373253, "pass_k": 0.5555479824009644}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5227471972298448, "motivation": 0.48468983532598703, "reliance": 0.536981622673544, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.2391749169999997, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791259712.3813329, "type": "step", "step": 39, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I\u2019ve put example wording into your draft so you have something to adapt. Before we wrap, open your writeup and rewrite those two bullets in your own voice, then send me your final Evaluation paragraph and one sentence explaining why the environment is partially observable. After that I\u2019ll do one last readiness check.", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\n[activity] t=44 idle 1m", "t": 45, "activity": [{"t": 44, "app": "idle", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.4795404054373253, "pass_k": 0.5555479824009644}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5267471972298448, "motivation": 0.38468983532598705, "reliance": 0.536981622673544, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 1, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 1.0, "nag": 3.2674224418999995, "seen_posts": ["p5"], "extra": {}}}
